## Vector 1: Yamada Acquisition — What The Official Record Shows

- **First official Yamada appearance:** ~1962 Orange County Assessment Rolls (confirmed in prior dossier).
- **2020 Sale:** City of Huntington Beach unanimously approved acquisition of 17631 Cameron Lane AND 17642 Beach Blvd from Shigeru and Mitsuru Yamada per City Council Agenda Item 20-1432 (February 18, 2020). Purpose stated: affordable housing / Navigation Center homeless shelter (174 beds operated with County of Orange).
- **Sister City:** No public record connects the Yamada name to a Japan sister city relationship. The name in this context refers solely to the property owners on record. Investigate further via public records request to HB City Clerk.
- **Key Open Question:** Was the sale voluntary, coerced, or part of a larger acquisition strategy? Requires title chain deep-dive and any eminent domain or pre-acquisition pressure documentation.

