## Vector 3: Good Neighbor Policy — What The Official Record Shows

- The HB "Good Neighbor Policy" in public records refers to short-term rental (STR) behavioral guidelines and group home / sober living facility regulations.
- The City has separate ordinances restricting public camping, loitering, and park use — distinct from any "Good Neighbor Policy" label.
- HB declared itself a non-sanctuary city (federal immigration enforcement cooperation).
- **Key Open Question:** The specific Good Neighbor Policy referenced in the investigation — applied to Navigation Center residents — requires the actual Navigation Center operational rulebook and intake paperwork to be pulled and examined for movement restriction language.

