## Vector 4: Civil Rights / Movement Restriction — What The Official Record Shows

- ACLU SoCal filed December 2020 lawsuit against Orange County and cities of Anaheim and Santa Ana (NOT Huntington Beach directly) for conditions at Bridges at Kraemer Place, La Mesa, and The Courtyard shelters — citing California Constitution violations of freedom of movement, privacy, and freedom from retaliation.
- No specific filed civil rights lawsuit naming Huntington Beach Navigation Center for freedom of movement violations found in public record to date.
- **Key Open Question:** Whether the Navigation Center's operational rules (intake, sign-in/sign-out, curfew enforcement, geographic restriction) constitute de facto confinement requires the actual operational policies from the Navigation Center operator (Mercy House) and OC County.

